# RENAME THIS FILE TO "local.properties" (remove ".template") BEFORE BUILDING.
#
# This file is machine-specific — every developer/computer needs their own
# copy pointing at where Flutter and the Android SDK are installed on
# THEIR computer. That's why it's not committed/shared as a real file.
#
# Usually you do NOT need to create this by hand: running any `flutter`
# command (e.g. `flutter pub get`) in this folder auto-generates a correct
# local.properties for you. Only edit manually if that fails.
#
# Example (Windows):
# sdk.dir=C\:\\Users\\YourName\\AppData\\Local\\Android\\sdk
# flutter.sdk=C\:\\src\\flutter
#
# Example (Mac):
# sdk.dir=/Users/YourName/Library/Android/sdk
# flutter.sdk=/Users/YourName/flutter
